Rotational invariance makes the statement independent of direction. For any unit vector $\mathbf n$, $\expect{\boldsymbol{\sigma}\cdot\mathbf n}
=\expect{\boldsymbol{\tau}\cdot\mathbf n}=0,
\qquad
\expect{
(\boldsymbol{\sigma}\cdot\mathbf n)
(\boldsymbol{\tau}\cdot\mathbf n)
}=-1.$ More generally, $\expect{\sigma_i\tau_j}=-\delta_{ij}.$ Each part is completely unpolarized, while equal-axis outcomes are perfectly anticorrelated.

