The rotationally invariant two-spin operator $\boldsymbol{\sigma}\cdot\boldsymbol{\tau}
=\sigma_x\tau_x+\sigma_y\tau_y+\sigma_z\tau_z$ organizes the four-dimensional state space. On the singlet, $(\boldsymbol{\sigma}\cdot\boldsymbol{\tau})\ket{S}
=-3\ket{S},$ while each of the three triplet states has eigenvalue $+1$.

