p.src:
Return to Alice’s local expectation value: $\expect{L_A}
=\sum_{a',a,b}
\Psi^*(a',b)L_{a'a}\Psi(a,b).$ Regroup the factors that do not belong to $L$: $\expect{L_A}
=\sum_{a',a}
\left[
\sum_b\Psi(a,b)\Psi^*(a',b)
\right]L_{a'a}.$ The expression in brackets is Alice’s reduced density matrix, $(\rho_A)_{aa'}
=\sum_b\Psi(a,b)\Psi^*(a',b).$ In basis-independent notation, $\rho_A
=\operatorname{Tr}_B\ket{\Psi}\bra{\Psi},$ and every Alice-local expectation value is $\expect{L_A}
=\operatorname{Tr}_A(\rho_A L).$

