p.src:
For a product state $\Psi(a,b)=\psi_A(a)\phi_B(b)$, $\begin{aligned}
(\rho_A)_{aa'}
&=\sum_b
\psi_A(a)\phi_B(b)
\psi_A^*(a')\phi_B^*(b) \\
&=\psi_A(a)\psi_A^*(a')
\sum_b|\phi_B(b)|^2 \\
&=\psi_A(a)\psi_A^*(a').\end{aligned}$ Thus $\rho_A=\ket{\psi_A}\bra{\psi_A}.$ This is a rank-one projector. Acting on $\ket{\psi_A}$ gives $\rho_A\ket{\psi_A}
=\ket{\psi_A}\braket{\psi_A}{\psi_A}
=\ket{\psi_A},$ while for every $\ket{\chi}$ orthogonal to $\ket{\psi_A}$, $\rho_A\ket{\chi}
=\ket{\psi_A}\braket{\psi_A}{\chi}
=0.$

