p.src:
Once the apparatus is admitted as a quantum system, there is no natural reason to stop there. Light from the pointer interacts with an eye; signals from the eye become correlated with a brain; an observer may be watched by another observer. Schrödinger’s cat and Wigner’s friend dramatize the same nested structure: $\begin{gathered}
\text{spin}
\longrightarrow
\text{apparatus}
\longrightarrow
\text{cat}\\
\longrightarrow
\text{Schr\"odinger}
\longrightarrow
\text{Wigner}.
\end{gathered}$ Inside any chosen boundary, one may describe the chain by unitary evolution and increasing entanglement. Outside the boundary, one uses the outcome-conditioned language of collapse.

